_values": ["Gothic horror, photorealistic 2D digital painting, a 19-year-old East Asian female bride with long dark hair partially obscured by a heavy red satin veil adorned with gold embroidery and a large bow, seated at a wooden table in a dimly lit, decaying interior space decorated with origami cranes and sunflowers, holding a torn red paper heart dripping with simulated blood while a zombie-like male figure with pale makeup and a red cloth gag stands behind her, adjusting the veil with both hands.  \nShe is a 19-year-old East Asian female with long, straight, dark hair cascading over her shoulders, her face painted with theatrical horror makeup featuring darkened eyes and streaks of red pigment resembling blood running down her cheeks; she wears a white lace-trimmed blouse beneath a voluminous red satin veil with intricate gold floral embroidery and a large, structured bow at the center; her posture is upright yet passive as she holds the torn red paper heart with both hands, positioned centrally in the frame, with the zombie figure standing behind her, gripping the veil’s edges, his dark clothing and pale, smeared makeup contrasting with the vivid reds of her attire and the origami decorations.  \nThe scene is set in a cluttered, aged interior with peeling wallpaper, dark wooden furniture, and a cluttered tabletop scattered with origami cranes in multiple colors, sunflowers, and a small doll, creating a shallow depth of field that blurs the background while keeping the subject and immediate foreground in sharp focus; the composition is centered on the seated female subject with the zombie figure positioned slightly off-center behind her, captured from a medium shot with a slight low-angle perspective to emphasize her vulnerability and the looming presence of the figure behind her, using a moderate focal length to maintain spatial clarity and emotional tension.  \nLow-key photography with dramatic chiaroscuro lighting, where the primary illumination originates 